        "original_id": "dc768c83-4b69-5f37-bc3f-d728df27e48f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michele Sindona, Nick Tosches, Giorgio Ambrosoli\n- Organizations: Gambino crime family, Vatican Bank, Franklin National Bank\n- Places: Long Island, New York, Franklin Square\n- Products: Power on Earth\n- Topics: banking, organized crime, murder\n\nFacts:\n- Franklin National Bank was based in Franklin Square on Long Island, New York.\n- Franklin National Bank was once the 20th largest bank in the United States.\n- Nick Tosches wrote Power on Earth as a biography of Michele Sindona.\n- Michele Sindona was a Mafia-linked Italian banker and an accused murderer.\n- Power on Earth details Michele Sindona's connections with the Gambino crime family, the Vatican Bank, and Franklin National Bank.\n- Power on Earth also covers the murder of Giorgio Ambrosoli, the lawyer overseeing the liquidation of Michele Sindona's banks.",
